Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 10:01:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/62] verimark: log the 0x99 match no-match response shape at
 info level

Triple verify-no-match on the IT with the correctly-enrolled
finger suggests the driver may be reading the verdict from a
mismatched offset/structure rather than a real bad match. The
current fp_dbg log only fires at debug verbosity, hiding the
firmware status code and the response payload prefix.

Promote the no-match path to fp_info and include the status word
plus the first 8 payload bytes. If the IT firmware uses an IT-
specific verdict code (analogous to enroll's 0x8006 = complete),
it'll surface here on the next attempt.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index cbf75d7..d2b8064 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -1191,8 +1191,20 @@ vfy_cb_match(GObject *src, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
         fp_info("verify: positive verdict on attempt %d (%zu bytes)",
                 ctx->attempt, payload_len);
     } else {
-        fp_dbg("verify: attempt %d no-match (status 0x%04x, %zu bytes)",
-               ctx->attempt, status, payload_len);
+        /* Logged at info level so the firmware status/payload shape is
+         * visible without a debug rebuild — useful for finding IT-
+         * specific match-on-chip codes (similar to enroll's 0x8006). */
+        fp_info("verify: attempt %d no-match (status 0x%04x, %zu bytes, "
+                "first 8 = %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x)",
+                ctx->attempt, status, payload_len,
+                payload && payload_len >= 1 ? payload[0] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 2 ? payload[1] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 3 ? payload[2] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 4 ? payload[3] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 5 ? payload[4] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 6 ? payload[5] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 7 ? payload[6] : 0,
+                payload && payload_len >= 8 ? payload[7] : 0);
     }
     g_free(payload);
     fpi_ssm_next_state(ssm);
